1. INTRODUCTION 
 
This report is based on data collected during the population census enumeration: 22 November 2009 
was the census day. The main purposes of this report are to: 
 
 provide a general overview of the 2009 census enumerations;  
 generate interest, curiosity, and a desire for more detailed information which can be used for 
specific analysis and the generation of topical census monographs; 
 advocate for the use of census data as a key source of statistical information for evidence 
based policy making; and  
 enhance the decision-making process of  policy-makers. 
 
This volume concentrates on making the enormous wealth of information incorporated in the Basic 
Tables accessible to user. This is done by providing summaries, figures and commonly used 
indicators (see Summa ry of main Indicators), and by making population projections and analyzing 
trends, especially trends with policy implications. 
 
For further information please contact the Solomon Islands National Statistics Office. 
 
